Abstract: RDF Time Series Sources describes how to connect your RDF knowledge graph to your time series. The readings stay compact: inside the metadata, as one small RDF node per reading or as one JSON literal, or in an external data file. RDF describes the source (where its readings are, which period they cover, whether readings may still be added) and each of its fields (the datatype of its values, where they are in a data file or JSON row, how they are stated, and what they observe, in which unit, with which sensor). The readings can be summarised and expanded into RDF points, which are aligned with SOSA and SAREF observations.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css no
Boilerplate: conformance no
